// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_lnx_av_kaspersky_av_disabled.yml
// ID Sigma: 36388120-b3f1-4ce9-b50b-280d9a7f4c04
// Título: Kaspersky Endpoint Security Stopped Via CommandLine - Linux
// Descripción: Detects execution of the Kaspersky init.d stop script on Linux systems either directly or via systemctl.
This activity may indicate a manual interruption of the antivirus service by an administrator, or it could be a sign of potential tampering or evasion attempts by malicious actors.

// Aplica a: Producto: linux | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: linux
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: high
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\linux\process_creation\proc_creation_lnx_av_kaspersky_av_disabled.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/systemctl" or FolderPath endswith "/bash" or FolderPath endswith "/sh") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "stop" and ProcessCommandLine contains "kesl")
